    "details": {
      "cr": 0.125,
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid"
      },
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>EGLATH ASHLUNG — CR 1/8 goliath escaped mine-slave, <strong>near-noncombatant</strong>. Hauled the dead out of the shafts for Dhul Maldur. He is the one who wanted everyone freed; the column died for it and he lived. Guilt-eaten, begs the party to go back. Replaces Faelan Mirith as the Ashlands runner.</p><p><strong>Rescue hook:</strong> he knows the holding pen — the rest of the column is at the staging mine near Dhul Maldur.</p><p><strong>Manual — Powerful Build:</strong> counts as one size larger for carrying capacity.</p><p><strong>Manual — Exhausted &amp; starved:</strong> disadvantage on STR &amp; CON checks and saves.</p><p><strong>Manual — Won't fight (RP):</strong> runs, shoves, refuses to fight if he can run at all. Acts only if cornered or if someone else is about to die.</p><p><strong>Manual — Hauler's Heave:</strong> the 10-ft push has no roll and no automation — move the target's token yourself.</p>"
      }
    }
  },
